{%- comment -%}
  Screens: cancellation flow (1 choose subscription → 2 before you cancel →
  3 why you started → 4 facts & alternatives → 5 cancellation reason →
  6 retention → 7 confirm → 8 cancelled), reactivation, inactive list,
  empty account.

  Ported from the approved Claude Design mockup ("VetPets Portal V2"),
  which frames step 1 as choosing WHICH SUBSCRIPTION to cancel, on the
  premise that every product is its own subscription. Phoenix has no such
  thing: one subscription, holding one or more product lines, and
  cancel(id) always ends the whole thing — there is no per-line cancel.
  See cancel-choose below for how that is reconciled, and cancel-confirm /
  cancelFacts in subscription-portal.js for where it matters most: the
  screen the customer commits on must never suggest that only one product
  is affected.

  Where a real subscription holds exactly one product, that product is
  named directly on the started/reason/retention screens (see
  cancel.focusName / cancel.reasonHeading / cancel.startedHeading in
  viewModel()) — the vast majority of accounts. A multi-product
  subscription falls back to generic "Routine Care" wording on those same
  screens, because there is no honest way to speak for the whole
  subscription in the name of just one of its products.

  Cancellation stays completable throughout: the save-offers are shown
  once, and "continue cancellation" is always present.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%} ---------- 1 · Choose subscription ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%}
  Always renders, even for the single-subscription majority — this is the
  screen the founder asked not to skip. It is deliberately NOT a picker:
  there is one real subscription, shown as one card (pre-selected, and the
  only option), listing every product inside it. Nothing here implies a
  product could be selected and cancelled on its own; the subtitle says so
  outright, replacing the design's own subtitle ("Each product in your
  routine is its own subscription"), which is not true of this data model.
{%- endcomment -%}
<section class="spp__screen" data-spp-screen="cancel-choose" hidden aria-labelledby="spp-cc0-h">
  <button type="button" class="spp__back" data-spp-go="subscription">
    {% render 'spp-icon', icon: 'chevron-left' %}Subscription
  </button>

  <div class="spp__narrow">
    <h1 class="spp__h1" id="spp-cc0-h">Which subscription do you want to cancel?</h1>
    <p class="spp__lede">
      This is the subscription tied to your account. Everything in it is reviewed
      together on the screens that follow.
    </p>

    <div class="spp__choices" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Your subscription">
      <div class="spp__choice spp__choice--stacked spp__choice--sub" role="radio" aria-checked="true" aria-disabled="true">
        <span class="spp__radio" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="spp__choice-text">
          <b>Routine Care subscription</b>
          <span>
            Every <span data-spp-field="subscription.intervalDays">60</span> days ·
            next <span data-spp-field="subscription.nextOrderShort">Sep 8</span>
          </span>
          <span class="spp__choice-products" data-spp-list="lineThumbs2">
            <template data-spp-tpl="lineThumbs2">
              <span class="spp__thumb spp__thumb--sm" data-spp-thumb><img data-spp-img alt=""></span>
            </template>
          </span>
          <span class="spp__choice-summary" data-spp-field="subscription.quantitySummary">FreshWipes ×2, EyeWipes ×1</span>
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <button type="button" class="spp__btn spp__btn--primary" style="margin-top:18px;" data-spp-go="cancel-benefits">Continue</button>
    <div class="spp__quiet-row">
      <button type="button" class="spp__btn spp__btn--link" data-spp-go="subscription">Never mind, take me back</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{%- comment -%} ---------- 2 · Before you cancel ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
<section class="spp__screen" data-spp-screen="cancel-benefits" hidden aria-labelledby="spp-cb-h">
  <button type="button" class="spp__back" data-spp-go="subscription">
    {% render 'spp-icon', icon: 'chevron-left' %}Subscription
  </button>

  <div class="spp__narrow">
    <div class="spp__pill spp__pill--info">Important: before you cancel</div>

    <div class="spp__info spp__info--icon" style="margin:14px 0;">
      {% render 'spp-icon', icon: 'clock-action', size: 19 %}
      <p>
        <b>95% of VetPets customers see meaningful results after 90 days</b> of consistent
        daily use. Daily care takes consistency, and your dog may also need time to become
        comfortable with the routine &mdash; giving it the full 90 days gives both the product and
        your pet a fair chance.
      </p>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      "4.8/5 · Trusted by 45,000+ Dog Owners" is the same real, already-
      approved aggregate rating used on the EyeWipes/FreshWipes offer and
      prelander pages — reused here in place of the design's own reviews
      carousel, which quotes a named, verified individual customer. There
      is no such real, attributable quote in this codebase to show
      instead, and inventing one is exactly the kind of fabrication this
      portal avoids everywhere else (see the vet-video note just below).
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="spp__trustbar">
      <span class="spp__trustbar-stars" aria-hidden="true">&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;&#9733;</span>
      <span>4.8/5 &middot; Trusted by 45,000+ Dog Owners</span>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      Veterinarian introduction video — a replaceable config value, never a
      fabricated video. data-spp-vet-video-url (root element, from
      section.settings.vet_video_url) is empty by default, in which case
      this stays exactly the static image it always was. Only when a real
      video URL is set in the theme editor does init() in
      subscription-portal.js swap [data-spp-vet-video] in for the image —
      see applyVetVideo() there. Nothing renders here until that setting is
      filled in with an actual, hosted video.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="spp__eyebrow" style="margin-top:18px;">Watch &middot; about 90 seconds</div>
    <h2 class="spp__h2" style="margin-top:4px;">Why consistency matters</h2>
    <div class="spp__media-16x9" data-spp-vet-media style="margin-top:10px;">
      <img
        data-spp-vet-image
        src="{{ 'spp-cancel-benefits.png' | asset_url }}"
        alt="A dog resting, waiting for its daily care routine"
        width="1280" height="720" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
      <div data-spp-vet-video hidden></div>
    </div>

    <button type="button" class="spp__btn spp__btn--primary" style="margin-top:20px;" data-spp-go="subscription">Never mind, keep my Routine Care</button>
    <div class="spp__quiet-row">
      <button type="button" class="spp__btn spp__btn--link" data-spp-go="cancel-started">Continue cancellation</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{%- comment -%} ---------- 3 · Why you started ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%}
  New screen — the approved design's "why you started" categorisation.
  Soft and non-blocking: the pick (data-spp-pick="startedCategory") only
  drives this row's own selected styling, is never sent to Phoenix, and
  never personalizes any later screen. What DOES personalize later screens
  is the subscription's real product data, named directly in the eyebrow
  line below (cancel.startedHeading) — see the file-level comment at top.
{%- endcomment -%}
<section class="spp__screen" data-spp-screen="cancel-started" hidden aria-labelledby="spp-cs-h">
  <button type="button" class="spp__back" data-spp-go="subscription">
    {% render 'spp-icon', icon: 'chevron-left' %}Subscription
  </button>

  <div class="spp__narrow">
    <div class="spp__eyebrow-row">
      <span class="spp__next-thumbs" data-spp-list="lineThumbs2">
        <template data-spp-tpl="lineThumbs2">
          <span class="spp__thumb spp__thumb--xs" data-spp-thumb><img data-spp-img alt=""></span>
        </template>
      </span>
      <span data-spp-field="cancel.startedHeading">Cancelling &middot; your Routine Care subscription</span>
    </div>

    <h1 class="spp__h1" id="spp-cs-h">What originally made you start using VetPets?</h1>
    <p class="spp__lede">Choose the main area you wanted help caring for.</p>

    <div class="spp__choices" role="radiogroup" aria-label="What you wanted help caring for" data-spp-list="startedCategories">
      <template data-spp-tpl="startedCategories">
        <button type="button" class="spp__choice spp__choice--stacked" role="radio" aria-checked="false" data-spp-pick="startedCategory">
          <span class="spp__radio"></span>
          <span class="spp__choice-text">
            <b data-spp-field="name">Dental care</b>
            <span data-spp-field="subtitle">Bad breath, plaque or tartar buildup</span>
          </span>
        </button>
      </template>
    </div>

    <button type="button" class="spp__btn spp__btn--primary" style="margin-top:18px;" data-spp-go="subscription">Keep my subscription</button>
    <div class="spp__quiet-row">
      <button type="button" class="spp__btn spp__btn--link" data-spp-go="cancel-alt">Continue cancellation</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{%- comment -%} ---------- 4 · Facts & alternatives ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
<section class="spp__screen" data-spp-screen="cancel-alt" hidden aria-labelledby="spp-ca-h">
  <button type="button" class="spp__back" data-spp-go="cancel-started">
    {% render 'spp-icon', icon: 'chevron-left' %}Back
  </button>

  <div class="spp__narrow">
    <div class="spp__pill spp__pill--info">Did you know?</div>

    <div class="spp__info spp__info--icon" style="margin:14px 0 12px;">
      {% render 'spp-icon', icon: 'clock-action', size: 19 %}
      <p>
        <b>95% of customers see meaningful results after 90 days</b> of consistent daily
        use. Daily care gives your dog time to become comfortable with the routine
        &mdash; and gives the product a fair chance.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="spp__tagrow">
      <span class="spp__tag">90 days</span>
      <span class="spp__tag">Once daily</span>
      <span class="spp__tag">Keep it simple</span>
    </div>

    <button type="button" class="spp__btn spp__btn--primary" style="margin-top:16px;" data-spp-go="subscription">I&rsquo;ll give it 90 days</button>
    <div class="spp__quiet-row">
      <button type="button" class="spp__btn spp__btn--link" data-spp-go="cancel-reason">Continue cancellation</button>
    </div>

    <h2 class="spp__h2" style="margin-top:28px;">You don&rsquo;t need to cancel to take a break</h2>
    <p class="spp__lede">
      Adjust your next delivery or ongoing schedule while keeping your Routine Care benefits.
    </p>

    {%- comment -%}
      The approved design shows three cards here: choose a delivery date,
      change delivery frequency, and contact support. Phoenix has no
      frequency/cadence change — "No cadence or frequency option appears,
      because Phoenix cannot perform one" is a rule already established
      elsewhere in this file (see the reschedule screen). The five proven
      schedule changes below stand in for the first card (every one maps
      to an operation verified end to end against Phoenix); the third card
      (Contact us for help) is reproduced as designed, real and unwired to
      anything but the honest "not available yet" data-spp-act="support"
      already used elsewhere in this portal.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="spp__choices" role="radiogroup" aria-label="How to move the next delivery" data-spp-list="gapOptions" style="margin-top:16px;">
      <template data-spp-tpl="gapOptions">
        <button type="button" class="spp__choice spp__choice--stacked" role="radio" aria-checked="false" data-spp-pick="gap">
          <span class="spp__radio"></span>
          <span class="spp__choice-text">
            <b data-spp-field="label">Skip the next delivery</b>
            <span data-spp-field="meta">Nothing ships. The one after is unchanged.</span>
          </span>
        </button>
      </template>
    </div>

    <div data-spp-gap-date hidden style="margin-top:14px;">
      <label class="spp__label" for="spp-gap-date">Pick a new delivery date</label>
      <input type="date" id="spp-gap-date" data-spp-date class="spp__input"
        aria-describedby="spp-gap-date-error"
        style="width:100%;box-sizing:border-box;min-height:48px;padding:12px 14px;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid rgba(13,35,64,.18);background:var(--spp-surface);font:500 15px/1.2 var(--spp-font);color:var(--spp-ink);">
      <p id="spp-gap-date-error" data-spp-date-error role="alert" hidden
         style="margin-top:6px;font:500 13px/1.4 var(--spp-font);color:var(--spp-danger,#B42318);"></p>
    </div>

    <p class="spp__fine">Same jar, same Routine Care price. You can move it again at any time.</p>

    <button type="button" class="spp__btn spp__btn--primary" data-spp-act="applyGap">
      <span data-spp-field="label.applyGap">Confirm this change</span>
    </button>

    <button type="button" class="spp__choice spp__choice--stacked" style="margin-top:12px;" data-spp-act="support">
      <span class="spp__choice-text">
        <b>Contact us for help</b>
        <span>Get help finding the best option for your routine.</span>
      </span>
    </button>

    <div class="spp__quiet-row">
      <button type="button" class="spp__btn spp__btn--link" data-spp-go="cancel-reason">Continue cancellation</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{%- comment -%} ---------- 5 · Cancellation reason ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
<section class="spp__screen" data-spp-screen="cancel-reason" hidden aria-labelledby="spp-cr-h">
  <button type="button" class="spp__back" data-spp-go="subscription">
    {% render 'spp-icon', icon: 'chevron-left' %}Subscription
  </button>

  {%- comment -%}
    Names the actual product — the sole one on a single-product account,
    or the generic fallback on a multi-product one — see
    cancel.reasonHeading in viewModel().
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <h1 class="spp__h1" id="spp-cr-h" data-spp-field="cancel.reasonHeading">Why are you cancelling?</h1>
  <p class="spp__lede">
    One question, then we&rsquo;ll finish the cancellation. Your answer helps us fix the routine for other owners.
  </p>

  <div class="spp__choices" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Cancellation reason" data-spp-list="reasons">
    <template data-spp-tpl="reasons">
      <button type="button" class="spp__choice" role="radio" aria-checked="false" data-spp-pick="reason" style="min-height:60px;border-radius:16px;justify-content:flex-start;gap:13px;">
        <span class="spp__radio"></span>
        <span data-spp-field="label">Too expensive</span>
      </button>
    </template>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    Shown only when "Something else" is chosen. The words are the point: a
    preset code tells us a category, this tells us what actually happened.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div data-spp-reason-note hidden style="margin-top:16px;">
    <label class="spp__label" for="spp-reason-note">Tell us what happened</label>
    <textarea id="spp-reason-note" data-spp-note rows="3" maxlength="1000"
      aria-describedby="spp-reason-error"
      placeholder="In your own words."
      style="width:100%;box-sizing:border-box;padding:12px 13px;border:1.5px solid rgba(13,35,64,.14);border-radius:12px;font:400 14.5px/1.5 var(--spp-font);color:var(--spp-ink);resize:vertical;"></textarea>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    Inline validation. Pressing Continue with nothing chosen used to do
    nothing at all, which reads as a broken button — the customer taps it
    again, harder, and still nothing happens.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <p id="spp-reason-error" data-spp-reason-error role="alert" hidden
     style="margin-top:12px;font:500 13.5px/1.45 var(--spp-font);color:var(--spp-danger,#B42318);"></p>

  {%- comment -%}
    Staying is the primary action, continuing is not. Both remain fully
    reachable: same order in the DOM as on screen, both real buttons, both in
    the tab sequence. Only the visual weight changes — nothing is hidden,
    disabled, or moved out of the keyboard path.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <button type="button" class="spp__btn spp__btn--primary" style="margin-top:18px;" data-spp-go="subscription">Keep my subscription</button>
  <div class="spp__quiet-row">
    <button type="button" class="spp__btn spp__btn--link" data-spp-act="reasonContinue">Continue cancelling</button>
  </div>
</section>

{%- comment -%} ---------- 6 · Retention ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%}
  THE ACCEPTANCE ACTION IS GATED.

  The screen renders exactly as approved, because the offer itself is
  approved. What is not established is whether the billing system can make it
  TRUE: no proven Phoenix operation discounts one delivery and then restores
  the standing price, and the Solvpath contract that comes closest carries no
  reversion semantics at all.

  So the button is real, the copy is real, and pressing it produces an honest
  "not available yet" rather than a success the next invoice would contradict.
  Connecting it is a server change; nothing on this screen moves.
{%- endcomment -%}
<section class="spp__screen" data-spp-screen="cancel-offer" hidden aria-labelledby="spp-co-h">
  <button type="button" class="spp__back" data-spp-go="cancel-reason">
    {% render 'spp-icon', icon: 'chevron-left' %}Back
  </button>

  <div class="spp__narrow">
    <div class="spp__media-16x9">
      <img
        src="{{ 'spp-cancel-offer.png' | asset_url }}"
        alt="A dog running, with the FreshWipes and EyeWipes jars"
        width="1280" height="720" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
    </div>

    <div class="spp__pill" style="margin-top:18px;">One-time offer</div>
    {%- comment -%}
      "Routine Care" is the fallback text of cancel.focusName — the same
      binding used on the reason screen — so a single-product account (the
      vast majority) reads exactly as before. A multi-product account sees
      the generic word instead of any one of its products, matching the
      approved design's "Before you go, 40% off your next FreshWipes
      delivery" heading as closely as this data model allows. It is
      wording only: the offer itself is whole-subscription, same as
      everything else on this screen.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <h1 class="spp__h1" id="spp-co-h">
      Before you go, <span data-spp-field="offer.percent">40</span>% off your next
      <span data-spp-field="cancel.focusName">Routine Care</span> delivery
    </h1>

    <div class="spp__card" style="margin:16px 0 14px;padding:16px;">
      <div class="spp__line" style="padding:0 0 12px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--spp-hair);">
        <span><b>Next delivery</b> &middot; <span data-spp-field="subscription.nextOrderShort">Sep 8</span></span>
        <b style="color:var(--spp-primary);font-size:19px;"><span data-spp-field="offer.percent">40</span>% off</b>
      </div>
      <div class="spp__line" style="padding:12px 0 0;">
        <span>Every delivery after that</span>
        <b><span data-spp-field="offer.standard">20</span>% off, as now</b>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="spp__lede" style="font-size:14.5px;">
      One delivery only. After it ships, your subscription returns to your usual
      Routine Care pricing &mdash; currently <span data-spp-field="offer.standard">20</span>% off.
    </p>

    <p class="spp__fine">
      Your Routine Care benefits &mdash; free shipping, flexible deliveries, the
      100-day guarantee &mdash; carry on unchanged.
    </p>

    <button type="button" class="spp__btn spp__btn--primary" data-spp-act="acceptOffer">
      <span data-spp-field="label.acceptOffer">Apply 40% to my next delivery</span>
    </button>
    <div class="spp__quiet-row">
      <button type="button" class="spp__btn spp__btn--link" data-spp-go="cancel-confirm">No thanks, continue cancelling</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{%- comment -%} ---------- 7 · Confirm ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
<section class="spp__screen" data-spp-screen="cancel-confirm" hidden aria-labelledby="spp-cc-h">
  {%- comment -%}
    data-spp-go is a fallback for a customer who somehow never eligible for
    JS at all; the real target is decided every render in
    renderCancelJourney(), because it depends on retentionOfferRedeemed,
    which can only be known once the subscription has loaded. A redeemed
    customer must land on the reason screen — the one immediately before
    the offer in the approved order — never back on the offer screen
    show() already refuses to display.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <button type="button" class="spp__back" data-spp-confirm-back data-spp-go="cancel-offer">
    {% render 'spp-icon', icon: 'chevron-left' %}Back
  </button>

  <div class="spp__narrow">
    {%- comment -%}
      No identifier here. The heading carried the subscription reference,
      which in live data is Phoenix's own subscription number — an internal
      identifier of a third-party billing system, shown to a customer who has
      exactly one subscription and therefore never needed it to tell which one
      they were cancelling.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <h1 class="spp__h1" id="spp-cc-h" style="margin-bottom:10px;">
      Cancel your subscription?
    </h1>
    <p class="spp__lede" style="line-height:1.5;">Here is exactly what happens if you confirm.</p>

    {%- comment -%}
      The first fact is the one that matters most here: cancelling this
      subscription ends EVERY product in it, not just whichever one was
      named on the earlier screens — see the 'cancelFacts' listData case,
      which states this explicitly whenever there is more than one product
      to disambiguate.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="spp__card spp__card--rows" style="margin-bottom:16px;padding:6px 18px;">
      <div data-spp-list="cancelFacts">
        <template data-spp-tpl="cancelFacts">
          <div style="display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:flex-start;padding:14px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--spp-hair);">
            <span style="flex:0 0 auto;margin-top:2px;color:var(--spp-accent);">
              {% render 'spp-icon', icon: 'check-circle', size: 19 %}
            </span>
            <p style="margin:0;font:500 14.5px/1.5 var(--spp-font);color:var(--spp-body);" data-spp-field="text"></p>
          </div>
        </template>
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      What they told us, shown back before they commit. A customer who picked
      the wrong reason a few screens ago can correct it here, and the record
      we keep is the one they actually meant.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="spp__line" data-spp-reason-row hidden
         style="background:var(--spp-surface-neutral,#F2FAFE);border-radius:14px;padding:14px 15px;margin-bottom:18px;">
      <span>
        <b style="display:block;">Reason on record</b>
        <span data-spp-field="reason.label" style="color:var(--spp-body);">Not given</span>
      </span>
      <button type="button" class="spp__btn spp__btn--link" style="min-height:40px;" data-spp-go="cancel-reason">Change</button>
    </div>

    <button type="button" class="spp__btn spp__btn--danger" data-spp-act="cancel">
      <span data-spp-field="label.cancel">Yes, cancel my subscription</span>
    </button>
    <button type="button" class="spp__btn spp__btn--secondary" style="margin-top:10px;min-height:52px;font-size:15.5px;" data-spp-go="dashboard">Keep my subscription</button>
  </div>
</section>

{%- comment -%} ---------- 8 · Cancelled ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
<section class="spp__screen spp__centred" data-spp-screen="cancel-done" hidden aria-labelledby="spp-cd-h">
  <div style="padding:26px 0;">
    <div class="spp__disc spp__disc--neutral">
      {% render 'spp-icon', icon: 'cancelled-check' %}
    </div>

    <h1 class="spp__h1 spp__h1--lg" id="spp-cd-h" style="margin-bottom:10px;">Your subscription is cancelled</h1>
    {%- comment -%}
      No identifier, and no promise about email.

      This paragraph named Phoenix's own subscription number — an internal id
      from a third-party billing system — and then promised a confirmation to
      an address it rendered from `customer.email`, which is not populated on
      this screen. Live customers read "A confirmation is on its way to ."

      Both are gone. The cancellation is stated as the fact it is, which needs
      neither an identifier nor an address to be true.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <p class="spp__lede" style="max-width:400px;margin:0 auto 22px;font-weight:400;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;">
      Your cancellation is confirmed.
      <strong style="color:var(--spp-ink);">No further charges will be made</strong> and nothing more will ship.
    </p>

    <div class="spp__card" style="max-width:460px;margin:0 auto 20px;text-align:left;border-radius:18px;box-shadow:none;">
      <div class="spp__line" style="padding:9px 0;font-size:14.5px;"><span>Last delivery</span><b>10 July 2026</b></div>
      <div class="spp__line" style="padding:9px 0;font-size:14.5px;"><span>Cancelled delivery</span><b><span data-spp-field="subscription.nextOrderShort">Sep 8</span> — not shipping</b></div>
      <div class="spp__line" style="padding:9px 0;font-size:14.5px;" data-spp-loyalty hidden><span>VetPoints kept</span><b><span data-spp-field="loyalty.points">640</span> for 12 months</b></div>
    </div>

    <button type="button" class="spp__btn spp__btn--primary" style="max-width:460px;margin:0 auto;" data-spp-go="reactivate">Reactivate subscription</button>
    <button type="button" class="spp__btn spp__btn--link" style="max-width:460px;margin:8px auto 0;" data-spp-go="inactive">View cancelled subscriptions</button>
  </div>
</section>

{%- comment -%} ---------- Reactivate ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
<section class="spp__screen" data-spp-screen="reactivate" hidden aria-labelledby="spp-re-h">
  <button type="button" class="spp__back" data-spp-go="inactive">
    {% render 'spp-icon', icon: 'chevron-left' %}Back
  </button>

  <h1 class="spp__h1" id="spp-re-h">Restart the routine</h1>
  <p class="spp__lede">Same products, same subscriber price. Pick when the first delivery should arrive.</p>

  <div class="spp__card">
    <div style="display:flex;gap:13px;align-items:center;padding-bottom:14px;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(13,35,64,.08);">
      <div class="spp__next-thumbs" data-spp-list="lineThumbs2">
        <template data-spp-tpl="lineThumbs2">
          <span class="spp__thumb spp__thumb--sm" data-spp-thumb><img data-spp-img alt=""></span>
        </template>
      </div>
      <div style="flex:1;min-width:0;font:600 15px/1.35 var(--spp-font);color:var(--spp-ink);">
        <span data-spp-field="subscription.quantitySummary">FreshWipes ×2, EyeWipes ×1</span>
        <span style="display:block;font:500 13.5px/1.4 var(--spp-font);color:var(--spp-muted);margin-top:3px;">
          <span data-spp-field="pricing.total">$62.73</span> per delivery
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div style="padding-top:16px;">
      <div style="font:600 13px/1 var(--spp-font);color:var(--spp-ink);margin-bottom:10px;">First delivery</div>
      <div class="spp__choices spp__choices--row" role="radiogroup" aria-label="First delivery" data-spp-list="restartDates">
        <template data-spp-tpl="restartDates">
          <button type="button" class="spp__tile spp__tile--wide" role="radio" aria-checked="false" data-spp-pick="restart">
            <span data-spp-field="label">As soon as possible</span>
          </button>
        </template>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <button type="button" class="spp__btn spp__btn--primary" style="margin-top:16px;" data-spp-act="reactivate">
    <span data-spp-field="label.reactivate">Reactivate subscription</span>
  </button>
</section>

{%- comment -%} ---------- Inactive list ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
<section class="spp__screen" data-spp-screen="inactive" hidden aria-labelledby="spp-in-h">
  <button type="button" class="spp__back" data-spp-go="dashboard">
    {% render 'spp-icon', icon: 'chevron-left' %}Overview
  </button>

  <h1 class="spp__h1" id="spp-in-h" style="margin-bottom:18px;">Cancelled &amp; inactive</h1>

  <div class="spp__grid spp__grid--wide" data-spp-list="inactiveSubs">
    <template data-spp-tpl="inactiveSubs">
      <div class="spp__card" style="border:1px solid rgba(13,35,64,.12);box-shadow:none;">
        {%- comment -%}
          The reference chip here was the same internal Phoenix id. The card
          already identifies the subscription the way a customer would — by
          product, cadence and the date it ended — so the id told them nothing
          they could use.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:flex-end;margin-bottom:14px;">
          <span class="spp__badge spp__badge--plain spp__badge--neutral" data-spp-field="statusLabel">Cancelled</span>
        </div>
        <div style="display:flex;gap:13px;align-items:center;margin-bottom:14px;">
          <span class="spp__thumb spp__thumb--muted" style="width:54px;height:54px;" data-spp-thumb><img data-spp-img alt=""></span>
          <div style="flex:1;min-width:0;">
            <div style="font:600 15px/1.3 var(--spp-font);color:var(--spp-ink);" data-spp-field="name">GloveWipes pack</div>
            <div class="spp__delivery-meta" data-spp-field="meta">Was every 30 days · cancelled 4 June 2026</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <button type="button" class="spp__btn spp__btn--secondary" style="min-height:48px;font-size:15px;" data-spp-go="reactivate">Reactivate</button>
      </div>
    </template>
  </div>
</section>

{%- comment -%} ---------- Empty account ---------- {%- endcomment -%}
<section class="spp__screen spp__centred" data-spp-screen="empty" hidden aria-labelledby="spp-em-h">
  <div style="padding:30px 0;">
    <div class="spp__disc spp__disc--lg" style="color:var(--spp-accent);opacity:.85;">
      {% render 'spp-icon', icon: 'paw', size: 44 %}
    </div>

    <h1 class="spp__h1" id="spp-em-h" style="line-height:1.25;margin-bottom:10px;">No subscriptions yet</h1>
    <p class="spp__lede" style="max-width:380px;margin:0 auto 22px;font-weight:400;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;">
      {%- comment -%} Identity-free: not a slot, so live mode cannot blank it. {%- endcomment -%}
      When you start a routine, it shows up here &mdash; with delivery dates and one-tap skip.
    </p>

    <button type="button" class="spp__btn spp__btn--primary" style="max-width:420px;margin:0 auto;" data-spp-go="dashboard">
      Browse the daily routine
    </button>

    <p style="margin:16px 0 0;font:500 14px/1.5 var(--spp-font);color:var(--spp-muted);">
      Ordered without an account? <a href="#" data-spp-go="account">Contact support</a> and we&rsquo;ll link it up.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
